post.description:
Any signed-in user. The response carries the full key, a secret that is
shown once and never again. The key's role may not exceed the caller's own;
asking for more answers 403.

put.description:
Admin or super admin. Both are replaced: a `color` left out clears it. 400
for a bad name or colour, 404 when the id is not a tag of this Organization,
409 when another tag has the name. Written to the audit log.

task_id.description:
The task queued, to poll with `GET /api/v1/endpoints/{id}/tasks/{task_id}`;
a repeat within a second answers the first call's task. Absent for
`verify_trust` and `migrate_to_machine`.

detect_how.description:
How `detect_name` is compared: `equals`, `starts_with` or `contains`.
Needed with `detect_name` for an EXE or MSIX with no detection rule yet;
an MSI is recognized by the codes in the file.
